    abstract = {Exact and asymptotic results for the uniform random labelled tree on \vphantom{\{}\}n\vphantom{\{}\} vertices have been studied extensively by combinatorialists. Here we treat asymptotics from a modern stochastic process viewpoint. There are three limit processes. One is an infinite discrete tree. The other two are most naturally represented as continuous two-dimensional fractal tree-like subsets of the infinite-dimensional space \vphantom{\{}\}l\_1\vphantom{\{}\}. One is compact; the other is unbounded and self-similar. The proofs are based upon a simple algorithm for generating the finite random tree and upon weak convergence arguments. Distributional properties of these limit processes will be discussed in a sequel.},
